{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1021788-houseruled-combo-mage-purified-possible-issues","id":1021788,"title":"Houseruled Combo, Mage + Purified. Possible issues?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-24T20:28:15-08:00","id":1021788,"title":"Houseruled Combo, Mage + Purified. Possible issues?","content":"Hello, so I am working on a campaign idea using the Sundered World setting from Dark Eras. My players will be Wise (that settings version of mage) who will later on be given the gift of Purification (pg 96 or so in the Immortals book) by a quest. While I am still thinking on just what I want available, I thought just leaving it as written and just adding it to the mage as an extra template. <br /> <br /> Obviously, there could be some lore issues and I know it says they cannot become mages but, for my game, I thought it would be an interesting dynamic because my players are starting play sometime around 5000 BCE. With Purified Siddhi for the most part being locked behind finding a spirit to teach them along with any numina, they would just be damn hardy Awakened. <br /> <br /> Another worry is the life span of an immortal Awakened and not letting it get out of hand. Though, I'm honestly open to a high power game. If the players buy up Arcana and stuff, why not? The game setting is mostly just a sandbox with a storyline thrown in for flavor. As a purified, they can be trapped or enslaved to account for large chunks of time. Maybe just treat gametime as active time with anything outside of that will see jumps in time regularly but I kinda want to just avoid Modern day all together or just prolong it so they can play around in history.<br /> <br /> Considering they need to buy mage things and purified things with the same xp I award, I don't think it would get too powerful. Especially when you are playing in a story where the long life span isn't that important, more for a way to see these guys survive antiquity.<br /> <br /> Comments, questions or suggestions? Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T20:39:30-08:00","id":1021791,"title":"","content":"If they're just hardy Awakened, why both with the Purified aspect at all?<br /> Also you can easily deal with the immortal aspect by just not letting them &quot;wait it out&quot;.<br /> Apply pressure, make them deal with problems in the now, if someone gets trapped, then they have to free them.<br /> <br /> Also unless you're forcing them to buy Purified abilities, and removing the opportunity for Arcane Experiences, there will be nothing which stops them advancing in power just as fast as most Awakened do.<br /> <br /> Also if all you want is for them to survive antiquity, you can just throw them into a high-dot Time spell to shunt them into the future. No need to bother with Purified stuff and messing with non-canon cross-template abilities at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T20:53:16-08:00","id":1021802,"title":"","content":"well I don't have just one reason in mind for the mix. The template of the Purified has always felt almost like a sub template. I just like some of the mechanics involved with it, having to mind your body even though you are immortal sounded interesting. This would be something the players get at the end of a story arc, a gift from a Pangean of the same caliber as Father Wolf.<br /> <br /> The story being based in the neolithic and knowing that I can now not have to hold any punches when it comes to combat. Death becomes another drama that story builds from. An enemy slays the party and takes the bodies away to be trophies, while the players are left as spirits that need to figure out how to fix things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T21:54:14-08:00","id":1021826,"title":"","content":"I read them few years back, but does not Purified are 'lesser template of Spirit mages'? Why then not give your Wise lot of Spirit related Mysteries and advise them to take like Adept of Spirit to let them be, practically, those immortal one Purified ( without using template itself )?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T23:24:05-08:00","id":1021857,"title":"","content":"Advice: don't try to mix rules. Just take what you want from the Purified, and translate it to Mage terms. You don't need to get rid of your idea, just to concentrate it into the main set of rules you'll be using.<br /> <br /> Mixed rules are an unnecessary pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T05:13:37-08:00","id":1021948,"title":"","content":"A Legacy inspired from the Purified and based on how they work, not necessarily about becoming Purified, could work. It helps that &quot;Siddhi&quot; literally means &quot;Achievement&quot; or &quot;Attainment&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T05:49:52-08:00","id":1021954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1021788-houseruled-combo-mage-purified-possible-issues?p=1021948#post1021948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Legacy inspired from the Purified and based on how they work, not necessarily about becoming Purified, could work. It helps that &quot;Siddhi&quot; literally means &quot;Achievement&quot; or &quot;Attainment&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah this is what I decided to do cause I wanted to exclude some things in the purified template anyway. Thanks for the input everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T08:12:19-08:00","id":1021987,"title":"","content":"i think that making a legacy that's just about becoming immortal is kind of a waste. The Tremere were the original idea for that and look how revamped they got in Left Hand Path.<br /> <br /> I'd actually recommend granting the players immortality via a Pact of Vassalage or something similar. That way you can basically have the goodness of the Pure along with a possible source of plot material from whoever holds their contract.<br /> <br /> Or provide more than one way to achieve immortality and that way you aren't shoe-horning your players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T10:17:00-08:00","id":1022026,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it is better to make the effect into a working rote or whatnot from another party, instead of a Legacy.<br /> <br /> If you make it into a Legacy, you'll be forcing your players about a major decision for character development, and utterly removing from them option about a future Legacy they could really want.<br /> <br /> Just DON'T make your decision trumps your players' freedom, unless you're really sure of your group's dynamics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:49:36-08:00","id":1023271,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think I am going to tear apart the Purified Template and make something special that fits into the lore of my setting, since my players are going to be in a world before the Gauntlet fell and Father Wolf still roams the Border Marches, maybe more is possible. I'm hoping to include it as a vision they receive after witnessing their tribesmen and others slay a Pangean and take its heartstone, they'll get a seed of thought that unravels as they grow up and they will hopefully be driven to follow the visions to the quest and other stuff.<br /> <br /> I thought at first to go with a Legacy but it really does limit things if I choose it for them or restrict them all together. This 'gift' is given by a mid ranking Pangean as a last ditch effort to save itself, picking a few 'chosen' from the crowd as it dies, the children of the expidition party.. just the players and a couple npcs..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}